    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/para[1]/text()",
      "slot": 8,
      "source": "A band marches down the field creating an amazing sound that bolsters the crowd. That sound travels as a wave that can be interpreted using trigonometric functions. For example, "
    },
    {
      "kind": "tail",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/para[1]/link[1]/tail()",
      "slot": 9,
      "source": " represents a sound wave for the musical note A. In this section, we will investigate trigonometric identities that are the foundation of everyday phenomena such as sound waves."
    },
    {
      "kind": "attribute:alt",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/figure[2]/media[1]/@alt",
      "slot": 10,
      "source": "Graph of a sound wave for the musical note A - it is a periodic function much like sin and cos - from 0 to .01"
