      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[3]/table[1]/tgroup[1]/tbody[1]/row[1]/entry[1]/emphasis[1]/text()",
      "slot": 103,
      "source": "Product-to-sum Formulas"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[3]/table[1]/tgroup[1]/tbody[1]/row[2]/entry[1]/emphasis[1]/text()",
      "slot": 104,
      "source": "Sum-to-product Formulas"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[4]/title[1]/text()",
      "slot": 105,
      "source": "Key Concepts"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[4]/list[1]/item[1]/text()",
      "slot": 106,
      "source": "From the sum and difference identities, we can derive the product-to-sum formulas and the sum-to-product formulas for sine and cosine."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[4]/list[1]/item[2]/text()",
      "slot": 107,
      "source": "We can use the product-to-sum formulas to rewrite products of sines, products of cosines, and products of sine and cosine as sums or differences of sines and cosines. See "
    },
    {
      "kind": "tail",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[4]/list[1]/item[2]/link[1]/tail()",
      "slot": 108,
      "source": ", "
    },
    {
      "kind": "tail",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[4]/list[1]/item[2]/link[2]/tail()",
      "slot": 109,
      "source": ", and "
    },
    {
      "kind": "tail",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[4]/list[1]/item[2]/link[3]/tail()",
      "slot": 110,
      "source": "."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[4]/list[1]/item[3]/text()",
      "slot": 111,
      "source": "We can also derive the sum-to-product identities from the product-to-sum identities using substitution."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[4]/list[1]/item[4]/text()",
      "slot": 112,
      "source": "We can use the sum-to-product formulas to rewrite sum or difference of sines, cosines, or products sine and cosine as products of sines and cosines. See "
    },
    {
      "kind": "tail",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[4]/list[1]/item[4]/link[1]/tail()",
      "slot": 113,
      "source": "."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[4]/list[1]/item[5]/text()",
      "slot": 114,
      "source": "Trigonometric expressions are often simpler to evaluate using the formulas. See "
    },
    {
      "kind": "tail",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[4]/list[1]/item[5]/link[1]/tail()",
      "slot": 115,
      "source": "."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[4]/list[1]/item[6]/text()",
      "slot": 116,
      "source": "The identities can be verified using other formulas or by converting the expressions to sines and cosines. To verify an identity, we choose the more complicated side of the equals sign and rewrite it until it is transformed into the other side. See "
    },
    {
      "kind": "tail",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[4]/list[1]/item[6]/link[1]/tail()",
      "slot": 117,
      "source": " and "
    },
    {
      "kind": "tail",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[4]/list[1]/item[6]/link[2]/tail()",
      "slot": 118,
      "source": "."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/title[1]/text()",
      "slot": 119,
      "source": "Section Exercises"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/section[1]/title[1]/text()",
      "slot": 120,
      "source": "Verbal"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/section[1]/exercise[1]/problem[1]/para[1]/text()",
      "slot": 121,
      "source": "Starting with the product to sum formula "
    },
    {
      "kind": "tail",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/section[1]/exercise[1]/problem[1]/para[1]/math[1]/tail()",
      "slot": 122,
      "source": " explain how to determine the formula for "
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/section[1]/exercise[1]/solution[1]/para[1]/text()",
      "slot": 123,
      "source": "Substitute "
    },
    {
      "kind": "tail",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/section[1]/exercise[1]/solution[1]/para[1]/math[1]/tail()",
      "slot": 124,
      "source": " into cosine and "
    },
    {
      "kind": "tail",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/section[1]/exercise[1]/solution[1]/para[1]/math[2]/tail()",
      "slot": 125,
      "source": " into sine and evaluate."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/section[1]/exercise[2]/problem[1]/para[1]/text()",
      "slot": 126,
      "source": "Explain two different methods of calculating "
    },
    {
      "kind": "tail",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/section[1]/exercise[2]/problem[1]/para[1]/math[1]/tail()",
      "slot": 127,
      "source": " one of which uses the product to sum. Which method is easier?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/section[1]/exercise[3]/problem[1]/para[1]/text()",
      "slot": 128,
      "source": "Explain a situation where we would convert an equation from a sum to a product and give an example."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/section[1]/exercise[3]/solution[1]/para[1]/text()",
      "slot": 129,
      "source": "Answers will vary. There are some equations that involve a sum of two trig expressions where when converted to a product are easier to solve. For example: "
    },
    {
      "kind": "tail",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/section[1]/exercise[3]/solution[1]/para[1]/math[1]/tail()",
      "slot": 130,
      "source": " When converting the numerator to a product the equation becomes: "
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/section[1]/exercise[4]/problem[1]/para[1]/text()",
      "slot": 131,
      "source": "Explain a situation where we would convert an equation from a product to a sum, and give an example."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/section[2]/title[1]/text()",
      "slot": 132,
      "source": "Algebraic"
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/section[2]/para[1]/text()",
      "slot": 133,
      "source": "For the following exercises, rewrite the product as a sum or difference."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/section[2]/para[2]/text()",
      "slot": 134,
      "source": "For the following exercises, rewrite the sum or difference as a product."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "locator": "/document[1]/content[1]/section[5]/section[2]/para[3]/text()",
      "slot": 135,
      "source": "For the following exercises, evaluate the product for the following using a sum or difference of two functions."
    },
